// Axis Strategic Airforce Commitment Chart (§44.41). Per scenario, how many Game-Turns each Axis
// Malta Availability Level (I–IV) may be used for strategic bombardment of Malta (§44.23):
//   Unlimited = may be used any number of turns (Level I is always Unlimited when Malta is in play,
//   §44.25); Turns(n) = usable at most n Game-Turns; NotAllowed = na (not applicable/allowed).
// The Campaign Game row (§64.0) is the primary target and fully confirmed. Two cells were blank on
// the chart and are interpreted from the rules: Race-for-Tobruk Level IV = NotAllowed (blank), and
// Long-Retreat Level I = Unlimited (§44.25: Level I is always unlimited while Malta is in play).
// Levels are ordered [I, II, III, IV].
(
    scenarios: {
        "Campaign Game":       [Unlimited, Turns(25), Turns(12), Turns(12)],
        "Graziani's Offensive":[Unlimited, NotAllowed, NotAllowed, NotAllowed],
        "Race for Tobruk":     [Unlimited, Turns(6), Turns(3), NotAllowed],
        "Crusader":            [Unlimited, Turns(4), Turns(2), Turns(2)],
        "Last Chance":         [NotAllowed, NotAllowed, NotAllowed, NotAllowed],
        "Long Retreat":        [Unlimited, Turns(3), NotAllowed, NotAllowed],
    },
)
